#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:5
#: 0b693c559c28442a84d1ad9e9f18750b
msgid "Independent Watchdog and Crash Dump"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:7
#: 364c088d64d4455f9c25a1139dc9a187
msgid "ArduPilot enables the autopilot CPU's internal independent watchdog which causes the CPU to be reset and restarted if a peripheral or some piece of code takes too long to complete or \"hangs\" the CPU.  This may or may not save the vehicle if in flight or motion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:9
#: d428f688a9ff48e3bca1c6a4f7b3d6a8
msgid "While not recommended, this feature can be disabled by setting :ref:`BRD_OPTIONS<BRD_OPTIONS>` = 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:11
#: 7a98af730ab140b19b01d71bf968fe18
msgid "In the case of a \"HARD FAULT\" (e.g an illegal instruction, out of bounds memory access, etc.) before resetting, the watchdog handler code will log a \"WDG\" message to the onboard log, send a \"WDG\" text message to the GCS and attempt to write a crash_dump.bin file to the \"@SYS\" flash area.  This crash_dump.bin file contains the cpu state and registers for later analysis (See section below for more details). A \"HARD FAULT\" is extremely serious and should be reported to ArduPilot. The vehicle is probably not safe to fly until the cause is resolved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:13
#: 884ab6a0dd874fbea0d5bfef6666e8be
msgid "In ArduPilot-4.5.1 (and higher), if a crash_dump.bin file has been created, a pre-arm failure will warn the user and prevent arming.  The crash_dump.bin file can be erased by re-flashing the ArduPilot firmware to the autopilot or it can be ignored by setting the :ref:`ARMING_CRSDP_IGN<ARMING_CRSDP_IGN>` param to 1 (not recommended)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:20
#: 55455b79b5eb4c8d98b931626ae8a4ba
msgid "Reporting a Watchdog / Crash Dump"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:22
#: 1ae4231da37a4db1b2a88ad63b50f9af
msgid "Use Mission Planner or another GCS to download the crash_dump.bin file from the \"@SYS\" flash area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:27
#: 9cdefeac860543159a8b5554a9691bac
msgid "Download the dataflash log from the flight or operation that caused the crash dump to be created.  Information on downloading logs can be found :ref:`here <common-downloading-and-analyzing-data-logs-in-mission-planner>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:29
#: 0286913750da43fe92b151faa06e6cd2
msgid "If the dataflash log cannot be found, find the git-hash of the firmware.  This appears in the GCS's messages tab soon after startup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:34
#: fb6ddbf15b674eccad2c6455bf44dabd
msgid "Open `ArduPilot's support forum <https://discuss.ardupilot.org/>`__, find the category for your vehicle and software version (e.g. `Copter-4.6 <https://discuss.ardupilot.org/c/arducopter/copter-46/179>`__, `Plane-4.6 <https://discuss.ardupilot.org/c/arduplane/plane-4-6/182>`__, `Rover-4.6 <https://discuss.ardupilot.org/c/ardurover/rover-46/180>`__), create a \"New Topic\", include \"watchdog\" in the title and attach the crash_dump.bin file, log file and/or git-hash as described above.  If the files cannot be uploaded directly, please include a link to where they can be downloaded from."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:38
#: b4a92bf6512845cab75a0e482bfa19df
msgid "Determining that a Watchdog Reset Occurred"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:40
#: d16ed4103a5c45fab65ad6a5082b9eff
msgid "One way is by looking at the dataflash logs. If the log is filtered to show only the \"MSG\" messages it can be seen that some include the word, \"watchdog\". This is a clear indication that the previous log or flight ended with a watchdog reset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:45
#: fe2015c002c447b99a86cc1469710970
msgid "A WDOG log message should also appear with the following columns that may be useful for developers investigating the cause of the watchdog"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:47
#: a77cfec31783457f8026aaddd73701cd
msgid "Task: The scheduler task number OR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:49
#: fdc56167c9fa4788abd64c02b770fd0e
msgid "-1 if the main loop just received the next IMU sample"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:50
#: 3075467d96784c7396246234c1de9225
msgid "-2 if the fast loop had started"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:51
#: 0ffc16caeba54b8cb4266fd1ac15e2b8
msgid "-3 if the main loop was waiting for the next IMU sample"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:53
#: 140ff577d4ef4b65b9912ef1b6b0cde6
msgid "IErr : Mask of Internal Errors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:54
#: 2f31847796da4a188358138696b77c2b
msgid "IErrCnt : Internal Error Count"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:55
#: bcc16657750d4d1da6a93b8d844ad2b1
msgid "MavMsg : MAVLink message id of last processed message"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:56
#: 5d824bc578f34e5f87eab9b47c6f22dc
msgid "MavCmd : MAVLink COMMAND_LONG or COMMAND_LONG_INT message's command field from last processed message"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:57
#: 6f079c7c0e1a40a6a18cf03e4bdffaf2
msgid "SemLine : Source code line number if program is waiting for a semaphore or 0 if not waiting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:58
#: b9c302919432442da6572fec0ebe1158
msgid "FL : Fault Line, the source code line number where the fault occurred.  Note this does not specify the filename but it can still be useful"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:59
#: 6feedc364ef04e9a80d417c333d69076
msgid "FT : Fault Type (see `FaultType enum in AP_HAL_ChibiOS/system.cpp <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/hwdef/common/stm32_util.h#L144-L151>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:61
#: 6dbeb8c6e2654cbc9f70a7590ef712e2
msgid "1 = Reset"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:62
#: 47adb416e84240b7b04fb0f485237a99
msgid "2 = Non-Maskable Interrupt (aka NMI)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:63
#: 6f86be775fe247bb88e8359d193e0504
msgid "3 = Hard Fault (the most common)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:64
#: a18cf7d253f04de788c644809d7b15fc
msgid "4 = Memory Management Fault"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:65
#: 2c2dc54ac592459c962019f04513e3f2
msgid "5 = Bus Fault"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:66
#: fc3e5b694bf240fe9e83b7f95ddf9973
msgid "6 = Usage Fault"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:68
#: 0579cb36e11a4c40b77e053214cdd226
msgid "FA : Fault Address (in memory).  For example this would be 0 in case an attempt was made to read a byte using a nullptr"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:69
#: 580f8ab8ead841928e116c995f03ec67
msgid "FP : Thread Priority (see list of priorities starting with APM_MONITOR_PRIORITY in `AP_HAL_ChibiOS/Scheduler.h <https://github.com/ardupilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/Scheduler.h#L25>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-watchdog.rst:70
#: 7d542880ffb04e969dc65b0eb525283d
msgid "ICSR : Interrupt Control and State Register (see \"ICSR bit assignments\" in ST datasheets)"
msgstr ""
